<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jiao Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jiao Province, or Jiaozhou, was a province of the Chinese empire covering northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and, at times, parts of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, under dynasties from the Han to the Tang. Its centre lay in the Red River delta. Local revolts against its governors, such as that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-nam-de">Ly Bi</a> in 541, were frequent, and in 679 the Tang reorganised it as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> General to Pacify the South, or Annan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jiao-province.jpg" alt="Jiao Province" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 沧海微沤 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E4%BA%A4%E5%B7%9E264.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
